The ff-nucleic-OL24.lib has 3 extra entries in the velocities table for DTN.
ParmEd fails due to this even though they are ignored by Amber.  This may not
actually be a ParmEd bug since the entries shouldn't be in the file.  Here the
relevant file is copied and modified.

The leaprc for OL24 sources ff14SB instead of only defining its own residues.
To keep unwanted protein residues out of the XML, the relevant leaprc is copied
into place in the input file and modified to not load its library files.
